---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Immigration, Job and Relocation Disclaimer | Relocate Works"
  description="Important disclaimer: Relocate Works provides educational relocation research only and does not provide immigration, legal, tax, financial or employment advice."
  canonicalPath="/disclaimer"
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero page-hero-gradient">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Important Disclaimer</span>
        <h1>Immigration, job and relocation information disclaimer.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Relocate Works helps readers research relocation opportunities, but it does not replace official government sources, employer confirmation, licensed professionals, or personal due diligence.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container prose">
        <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> June 28, 2026</p>

        <h2>1. No legal immigration advice</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works is not an immigration law firm, licensed migration agency, immigration adviser, government agency, recruiter, employer, tax adviser, financial adviser, or relocation service provider. The information on this website is provided for general research and educational purposes only.
        </p>
        <p>
          You should not treat any Relocate Works page, job note, sponsor status, country guide, visa summary, salary note, tax overview, cost of living estimate, relocation company listing, or newsletter post as legal advice or personalized immigration advice.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Visa rules change frequently</h2>
        <p>
          Immigration programs, visa names, salary thresholds, occupation lists, employer requirements, government fees, processing times, and eligibility criteria can change at any time. A page that was accurate when written may become outdated later. Always verify visa information with official government websites and qualified professionals before making decisions.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Job listings and sponsor signals are not guarantees</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works may identify jobs that appear sponsor-friendly based on publicly available information. However, sponsorship depends on employer policy, candidate profile, location, role level, budget, compliance requirements, and timing. A job may be changed, paused, filled, removed, or limited to local candidates after publication.
        </p>
        <p>
          Terms such as sponsor-friendly, visa signal, relocation signal, confirmed, likely, unknown, relocation score, or sponsor confidence are internal research labels. They are not official statements from employers or governments unless the relevant source directly says so. Candidates must confirm details directly with employers or recruiters.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Salary, tax and cost of living information is approximate</h2>
        <p>
          Salary, tax and cost of living information can vary by city, role, seniority, lifestyle, family size, housing choice, exchange rate, insurance needs, visa status, and local regulations. Relocate Works may provide planning-level information, but it should not be used as financial, tax, accounting, or investment advice.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before relocating, candidates should prepare a personal budget, check current salary data, verify tax obligations, review healthcare and insurance requirements, and consider professional advice where appropriate.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Relocation companies and third-party providers</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works may mention relocation companies, job boards, newsletter platforms, payment providers, visa resources, housing resources, insurance providers, and other third-party services. Mentions do not necessarily mean endorsement. We are not responsible for third-party pricing, quality, availability, legal compliance, privacy practices, or service outcomes.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Candidate responsibility</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Verify job sponsorship details directly with employers before applying or accepting an offer.</li>
          <li>Check official immigration rules before spending money on applications, documents, tests, flights, housing, or relocation services.</li>
          <li>Understand that relocation decisions involve legal, financial, professional, personal, and family risks.</li>
          <li>Use Relocate Works as a research starting point, not as a final decision-maker.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. No outcome guarantee</h2>
        <p>
          Relocate Works does not guarantee job offers, interviews, visa sponsorship, visa approval, permanent residency, work authorization, salary levels, employer response, relocation support, or successful settlement in any country.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you notice outdated information, unclear wording, or a page that needs correction, please contact Relocate Works. We aim to improve the usefulness and clarity of the website over time.
        </p>

        <p class="legal-note"><strong>Important:</strong> If your decision involves immigration law, employment contracts, tax obligations, or large relocation costs, speak with qualified professionals and verify official sources before acting.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
